   303	## 6. Gate impact: what changes, what does not
   304	
   305	### Unchanged — every hard gate
   306	
   307	- The hard Preview gate. "Programs compiled from Moriarty source must produce
   308	  actual financial transactions whose finalized state and complete effects match
   309	  independent expectations." No refinement work touches
   310	  `spec/examples/loan.mori`, `spec/examples/swap.mori`,
   311	  `compact/generated/**`, or the deployed contract
   312	  `8034dffa6ce124cf34135799969d34831da5ce44fd287a3bead2fa3ce293a341`.
   313	- MC01 through MC08 acceptance text: all unchanged.
   314	- Every sprint exit gate: unchanged.
   315	- SP02's and SP03's entry gates: unchanged.
   316	- G01–G24 predicates in `legacy-release-gates.json`: unchanged verbatim.
   317	- Mandatory PCD: unchanged, undeferred, unconditioned.
   318	- The 277 ACTUS fixtures, 18 executable types, 32 dispositions, 72 DeFi rows,
   319	  DA01–DA24, three held-outs, eight intent cases, eight regression classes, five
   320	  composition operators, twelve additional report products: denominator
   321	  unchanged.
   322	
   323	### Gains content — three places, none of them a relaxation
   324	
   325	1. **SP02's "static specification" scope** now explicitly includes refinement
   326	   judgments. The exit gate wording is unchanged; the work behind it grows.
   327	2. **SP03.3's claim manifest** gains a refinement-soundness domain. An
   328	   undischarged claim there blocks SP03 completion, exactly as the existing
   329	   claims do. This makes SP03 harder, not easier.
   330	3. **G16's trusted-computing-base inventory** must name the solver. G16 already
   331	   "requires a named trusted computing base"; the inventory changes because the
   332	   TCB changes. Declaring it here rather than discovering it at SP12 is the whole
   333	   point of recording it.
   334	
   335	### Two new stop conditions
   336	
   337	- A source whose obligations are not discharged **does not compile**. There is no
   338	  warning mode, no `--skip-proofs`, no assumption escape.
   339	- A discharge certificate that does not match its obligation digest **rejects**.
   340	  It is never silently accepted as still valid.
   341	
   342	---
   343	
   344	## 7. Dependencies and what this unblocks
   345	
   346	```
   347	rp01-full (SP01.2 + SP01.3, admissible NOW, currently open)
   348	  |
   349	  +--> successor-frontend (SP02.1 .. SP02.4)   <-- /6 grammar, checker, CLI, discharge
   350	         |
   351	         +--> successor-semantics (SP03.3)     <-- refinement-soundness K claim
   352	                |
   353	                +--> actus-semantics (SP07)    <-- directional rounding refinements
   354	                +--> defi-semantics (SP08)     <-- SP08.4 refinement statement
   355	                       |
   356	                       +--> mandatory (SP09.2) <-- one more discharged obligation domain
   357	                              |
   358	                              +--> release (SP12) <-- G16 TCB, G12 reproducibility
   359	```
   360	
   361	**Unblocks, concretely:**
   362	
   363	- **SP07 at the right time.** Deciding law-versus-oracle before 277 ACTUS
   364	  fixtures are authored avoids writing them all as source postconditions and then
   365	  migrating them. This is the largest avoided cost in the whole proposal.
   366	- **SP08.4's existing "refinement statement" obligation** gets a concrete
   367	  referent instead of an undefined term.
   368	- **A measured proving-cost result** for `refinement-directed-lowering`: the
   369	  advisory analyser quantifies how many of the loan kernel's 19 asserts and the
   370	  swap kernel's 23 are fixture comparisons, without changing any bytes.
   371	
   372	**Does not unblock and must not be claimed to:** native recursion, mandatory PCD,
   373	Preview settlement, ACTUS conformance, private composition, release.
   374	
   375	---
   376	
   377	## 8. Sequencing rule
   378	
   379	**Rule R1.** The design half (SP01.2 and SP01.3 rows, and the read-only advisory
   380	analyser) may proceed now under the existing task contract. It is routine
   381	authorized local work and needs no new campaign, packet or allocation
   382	(`ROADMAP-REFINEMENT-2026-09-09.md` §"Apply the orchestration lessons").
   383	
   384	**Rule R2.** The implementation half enters at SP02's existing gate and not
   385	before. `rp01-full` must be reviewed first. No `/6` grammar, frontend, formatter
   386	or CLI work is admitted until then. A scheduler must use task entry gates, not
   387	whole-sprint completion (`sprints.json` `dependencyMeaning`).
   388	
   389	**Rule R3.** Refinement work never becomes a prerequisite of anything already
   390	scheduled. SP04, SP05, SP06, SP09.1 and SP10 keep their current entry conditions.
   391	
   392	**Rule R4.** No atomic-profile byte changes. A refinement-erased atomic profile,
   393	if ever wanted, is `moriarty-bounded-atomic/2` with its own full Preview lineage,
   394	and it is not started until SP05 aggregate reconciliation and SP09 mandatory
   395	acceptance have closed against `/1`.
   396	
   397	**Rule R5.** Stop conditions inherit unchanged. "Stop on the first failed required
   398	control, undefined essential interface or resource ceiling." An undischargeable
   399	obligation is a failed required control and stops the affected task; it does not
   400	authorise a warning mode.
   401	
   402	---
   403	
   404	## 9. Honest limitations of this delta
   405	
   406	- Everything above is **S2, specified-only**. No refinement checker exists. No
   407	  `/6` profile exists. No obligation has been discharged by any tool in this
   408	  repository.
   409	- The z3 results this rests on (Findings 1–7) are scoped experiments in
   410	  `scratchpad/aeon/`, not repository evidence. They are re-runnable and cited,
   411	  but they are not a reviewed deliverable and they do not establish that a
   412	  refinement checker is feasible at corpus scale.
   413	- The clause counts in `REQUIREMENTS.md` §2.1 are measured on a **draft** rewrite
   414	  that no parser has accepted, because no `/6` parser exists. They are a design
   415	  estimate, not a build result.
   416	- Adding a solver to the toolchain is a real reproducibility and TCB cost.
   417	  §REQUIREMENTS M13–M16 mitigate it; they do not eliminate it.
   418	- This delta is planning output. Per `ROADMAP-REFINEMENT-2026-09-09.md`: "A
   419	  planning document is the product of this user-requested planning turn; it does
   420	  not count as language implementation."
   421	
   422	---
   423	
   424	## 10. Validation
   425	
   426	After applying the delta, run the existing checks, which are the only authority
   427	on planning integrity:
   428	
   429	```sh
   430	python3 openspec/sprints/verify.py
   431	openspec validate --all --strict
   432	```
   433	
   434	`verify.py` "checks every declared task ID and compares those rows with the
   435	authoritative stage graph", so adding `SP02.4` to `sprints.json` without adding
   436	the task to `sp02-complete-mori-authoring-frontend.md` will fail. That is the
   437	intended behaviour. These checks verify navigation and coverage only. They do not
   438	execute a sprint or certify language behaviour.

