     1	# Adopt refinement types from Aeon in the Moriarty source language
     2	
     3	## Why
     4	
     5	Moriarty source states its obligations as fixture assertions, not as laws. A census of
     6	`experiments/moriarty-language/spec/successor/examples/*.mori` counts 64 `ensures` clauses,
     7	of which 40 compare against a literal constant. In `loan-lifecycle.mori` all 39 `ensures`
     8	clauses are non-laws: 8 restate a `next` write and 31 are fixture constants.
     9	
    10	Those constants hide unsound guards. An SMT encoding of the `repay` action in
    11	`loan-lifecycle.mori`, using its actual `requires` clauses and the AccrualFirst allocation
    12	implemented in `src/successor/repayment.ts`, satisfies every written guard while driving
    13	`principal` to `-1` and the borrower balance to `-1`. Ablation shows the two clauses that
    14	carry the safety argument are `nominal <= outstanding(...)` and `nominal <= balance(Borrower)`.
    15	Neither has a spelling in `moriarty-financial-agreement-source/5`. The one precondition the
    16	source does write, `requires payment > 0`, is not load-bearing.
    17	
    18	Aeon states such obligations in the type. A refinement carries a predicate, an SMT solver
    19	discharges it inside a decidable fragment, and the contract is proved before execution. This
    20	package adapts that design to Moriarty's bounded financial setting.
    21	
    22	The package can change the terminal evidence-gated decision because it supplies the static
    23	scope that SP02 leaves open, and the discharged claim domains that SP09.4 already requires.
    24	It does not supply Preview evidence and does not close any network gate.
    25	
    26	## What Changes
    27	
    28	- Add refinement predicates and named agreement invariants to a new source profile.
    29	- Define the decidable fragment, verification condition generation and discharge receipts.
    30	- Add linear and affine multiplicity for one-shot lifecycle rights and divisible budgets.
    31	- Define when a discharged obligation permits the compiler to specialize or omit a circuit gadget.
    32	- Define the migration of fixture clauses to laws, and of genuine oracles to test rows.
    33	
    34	## Capabilities
    35	
    36	### New Capabilities
    37	- `refinement-types`: `where` predicates, named invariants, subtyping, obligation schedule, erasure.
    38	- `verification-discharge`: fragment classification, VC generation, solver binding, receipts, diagnostics.
    39	- `linear-obligations`: multiplicity kinds, the intra/cross transaction seam, conservation laws.
    40	- `refinement-directed-lowering`: elimination tiers, gadget specialization, constraint budgets.
    41	- `specification-migration`: fixture-to-law migration, profile strategy, authoring surface.
    42	
    43	### Modified Capabilities
    44	None. Existing MC and sprint acceptance stays normative. `moriarty-bounded-atomic/1` and
    45	profiles `/1` through `/5` are not changed by this package.
    46	
    47	## Impact
    48	
    49	Primary ownership: `experiments/moriarty-language/spec/successor/**` and
    50	`experiments/moriarty-language/src/successor/**`. A new profile `/6` is additive.
    51	
    52	Explicit non-goals. This package does not change `moriarty-bounded-atomic/1`. The September 17
    53	Preview loan binds `spec/examples/loan.mori` by path in `deliverables/preview-loan-2026-09-17/
    54	build-run01/request.json` and by digest assertion in `custody/generate.mjs`. Any change to
    55	those bytes discards the only banked Preview financial evidence. Refinement work reaches the
    56	atomic profile only as a read-only advisory analyser that emits no artifact.
    57	
    58	This package does not weaken a gate, does not add a scheduler, and does not authorize a native
    59	retry. It does not close SP05, MC02, or mandatory PCD.
    60	
    61	Lifecycle: every requirement below is S2, specified only. No behavior in this package is
    62	implemented. Measurements cited are reproduced and named at their source.

