    10	4. The page linked the requirements agenda but gave no complete comparison. Added all 35 MPLR rows and all 24 backend/recursion rows, with local foundations and open obligations. No full requirement is marked satisfied by a partial local mechanism.
    11	5. Current implemented profiles do not define the full planned authenticated continuation, evidence, conditional settlement, phase, recovery, delegation or private history contracts. Added the required semantic interfaces as specified-only design. Their concrete syntax, typing/effect rules, Core encodings and proof obligations must be frozen under U0; labels on the page are not source keywords.
    12	6. Native proof, compiler, ledger, federation and service obligations require different enforcement points. Retained their ownership and required evidence rather than treating syntax additions or finite tests as backend assurance.
