51:**Authoritative context and fees (ZR03/10/11).** Publish which network/genesis identity, contract/operation, domain, time/expiry, read set, complete effects and phase fields come from the ledger and which are application commitments. Enforce their linkage. A committed prover-selected network or clock is not authoritative context. The signed maximum fee, denomination and permitted failure fee policy must be enforced at actual debit; exact fees decided later can be checked by the ledger against that cap instead of being fictitiously known during proving. Test cross-network replay, changed fee asset/recipient, phase relocation and stale reads. State which controls invalidate proof bytes and which fail ledger checks.
